note Back and forward, the way a browser does it. Nothing in the app calls a 'navigate' function: at the end of every frame, after the action queue has been applied, the current place is compared with the place at the end of the last frame, and if they differ the old one is pushed onto the history. So any click anywhere - a symbol in a list, a tab, an xref, a command in the output panel - becomes history for free, and no feature has to remember to record itself. A place is the centre tab, the current file, the line selection, the focused symbol as a stable key, and the selected path and step; a changed line selection alone does not count as a move. All of it lives in Nav, which only nav.rs changes.

